  "narrative": "The new independent validation for H48 is suggestive but not decisive. The discovery comparison within STK11-loss cells gave a signed estimate of about +0.031 (95% CI -0.010 to +0.073), and the independent validation gave a larger signed estimate of about +0.043 (independent 99.6% CI -0.024 to +0.109). Both point estimates are in the hypothesized direction—stronger KRAS dependency in KRAS-mutant cells relative to KRAS-wildtype cells within STK11-loss eligibility—and both exceed the approximate 0.025 absolute dependency-score scale that corresponds to a 10% relative difference on the observed negative-scale dependency outcomes. However, the intervals are wide, include null, include clinically subthreshold effects, and include at least some opposite-direction effect in the independent interval. Therefore, I do not accept H48 as evidence of a scientifically meaningful difference in this dataset. I keep it unresolved and active. The most plausible interpretation is that KRAS dependency may be enhanced in KRAS-mutant cells that have STK11 loss, but the subgroup sample and validation precision are insufficient for a confident conclusion. This remains an association claim, not a causal or externally generalizable mechanism. The next analyses should test whether the KRAS-mutation effect is genuinely concentrated in STK11-loss cells rather than being a broader KRAS-mutation effect diluted by small cell counts. I registered an interaction test comparing the KRAS-mutation effect in STK11-loss cells with the effect in STK11-intact cells, plus a direct complement estimate within STK11-intact cells. A positive interaction with a small or null complement effect would strengthen the case for context-specific KRAS/STK11 co-mutation biology in this dataset; a substantial complement effect would make H48 more consistent with a general KRAS-mutation association and would shift attention toward the overall KRAS claim and its precision. I also keep the STAT3/PTEN-loss robustness checks as high priority because PTEN loss showed a much larger accepted dataset association and still needs technical robustness assessment. H2 and H4 remain unresolved for similar precision/effect-size reasons rather than because of clear null evidence.",
  "research_notes": "Current accepted dataset associations: H5 SMARCA4 loss -> stronger SMARCA2 dependency; H7 MSI-high -> stronger WRN dependency; H20 KEAP1 loss -> weaker NFE2L2 dependency; H17 PTEN loss -> stronger STAT3 dependency. Robustness accepted/closed for key strata: H23/H24 library-stratified SMARCA2; H25/H43 Avana/high-Cas9 WRN; H26/H27 library-stratified NFE2L2. H39 null among SMARCA4-intact cells supports SMARCA4 specificity but is not proof. H2 remains unresolved after independent validation: discovery point near threshold but independent validation smaller and imprecise. H48 now has independent validation: signed discovery estimate +0.031 and signed validation estimate +0.043, both above the approximate 0.025 threshold proxy, but intervals cross null and subthreshold effects; unresolved and active. Next highest-value follow-ups: H62 interaction of KRAS-mutation effect by STK11-loss, H63 complement KRAS effect in STK11-intact cells, and STAT3 PTEN-loss robustness H57-H61. Secondary: direct EGFR/KRAS histology subgroup tests H29-H32 and MYC high-growth-rate refinements H49-H50 if capacity allows. H28 remains deferred because likely small non-Avana MSI-high cells. All conclusions are dataset associations, not causal or generalizable mechanisms."
}

