 "narrative": "This synthesis is the final scientific report for the current evidence in the supplied dataset.\n\nNew validation: H20 is independently validated and closed. KEAP1 loss is associated with weaker NFE2L2 dependency. Discovery R8 signed estimate +0.796 (95% CI +0.776 to +0.816); independent validation R79 signed estimate +0.829 (independent CI +0.800 to +0.857). Both intervals exclude zero even at stricter validation alpha and are far above any ~10% relative difference threshold for NFE2L2 dependency. Because more negative scores mean stronger dependency, positive signed estimates mean KEAP1-loss cells have higher/less negative NFE2L2 scores, i.e. weaker dependency. This corroborates rejection of the original opposite-direction H8 claim.\n\nResponse deadline H96: the KRAS mutation effect in STK11-loss, TP53-wildtype cells had discovery R50 +0.052 (CI +0.008 to +0.096), but validation R53 +0.017 (independent CI -0.058 to +0.092). The validation point is below the approximate 10% relative threshold and does not reproduce the discovery effect, although the interval remains compatible with a clinically meaningful effect. I leave H96 unresolved and closed rather than reject, but this KRAS co-mutation refinement is not accepted and should not be promoted.\n\nNew validation H69: BRAF V600E versus RIT1 dependency is null/uncertain. Discovery R35 +0.004 (CI -0.025 to +0.033) and validation R80 -0.002 (independent CI -0.043 to +0.039). Both are imprecise, though validation includes clinically meaningful positive values; leave unresolved and closed with no further follow-up.\n\nCurrent supported findings: independently validated dataset associations are H5 SMARCA4 loss with much stronger SMARCA2 dependency, H17 PTEN loss with stronger STAT3 dependency, H73 TP53 loss with weaker USP7 dependency, and H20 KEAP1 loss with weaker NFE2L2 dependency. H7 MSI-high with much stronger WRN dependency remains accepted on discovery and many robustness strata but is still the main core association not independently validated. All are observational associations among 2000 lung-cell-line profiles, not causal mechanisms or externally generalizable claims.\n\nNegative or unsupported results remain informative: BRAF V600E did not support stronger BRAF dependency; ERBB2 amplification did not support overall ERBB2 dependency or adenocarcinoma-specific enhancement; ARID1A loss did not support SMARCA2 dependency; MYC amplification did not support POLR2A or USP7 dependencies; overall EGFR amplification failed to validate as a clinically meaningful effect; overall KRAS dependency was not decisive; lineage heterogeneity for SMARCA4/SMARCA2 was not supported; NF1 loss did not support RIT1 dependency; TP53 loss did not support stronger DHX9 dependency in the original direction.\n\nUnresolved questions include conditional EGFR effects, KRAS co-mutation contexts after failed validation, formal lineage heterogeneity for USP7 and STAT3, research-marker/TMED10 signals, MYC-related RPL11 and KIF18A, TP53-MDM2 contexts, and BRCA2-related DHX9/WRN effects.\n\nMost informative next analysis: request independent validation of H7 MSI-high and stronger WRN dependency. If it validates, close the core MSI/WRN claim; if it fails, reassess H7 as a discovery-only robust-stratum association. Otherwise, remaining analyses are lower priority explorations.",
