  "narrative": "Independent validation resolves the main open questions from iteration 8. For H20, validation R79 confirms the KEAP1-loss/NFE2L2 association with a strict independent interval signed +0.829, lower bound +0.800 and upper bound +0.857; combined with discovery R8, I accept H20 and close it as independently validated. For H69, validation R80 is near zero and opposite the registered direction, signed -0.002 with independent interval -0.043 to +0.039. Together with discovery R35, there is no support for a clinically meaningful positive BRAF V600E association with RIT1 dependency; however, the validation interval still includes modest positive values around or above the approximate 10 percent clinical threshold, so I leave H69 unresolved and close it rather than claim a definitive null. For H140, validation R106 independently supports CDKN2A loss in TP53-wildtype cells with stronger MDM2 dependency, signed +0.112, lower bound +0.053 and upper bound +0.171, which is above the approximate 0.027 MDM2 clinical-threshold scale. Combined with discovery R88 and the accepted robustness strata H143-H146, I accept H140 and close it as an independently validated observational dataset association. H147 remains important context: the CDKN2A-MDM2 association is not strictly TP53-wildtype-specific, and H149 supports that it is not solely an MTAP co-deletion proxy. For H58, validation R107 strongly supports PTEN loss associated with stronger STAT3 dependency among non-Avana library cells, signed +0.358, lower bound +0.127 and upper bound +0.589, well above the STAT3 clinical-threshold scale. The imprecise discovery R28 is outweighed by the strict independent validation interval; I accept H58 and close it, adding library-context robustness to H17. Overall, the strongest dataset-supported associations are much stronger SMARCA2 dependency with SMARCA4 loss, much stronger WRN dependency in MSI-high cells, weaker NFE2L2 dependency with KEAP1 loss, stronger STAT3 dependency with PTEN loss, weaker USP7 dependency with TP53 loss, and stronger MDM2 dependency with CDKN2A loss in TP53-wildtype cells. These core associations are independently validated in the supplied validation set, and H58 additionally validates PTEN-STAT3 within non-Avana screens. Negative or limited findings remain for overall EGFR amplification, ERBB2 amplification, MYC amplification with POLR2A or USP7, PIK3CA mutation with STAT3 or EGFR, BRAF V600E with BRAF dependency, NF1 loss with BRAF or RIT1, ARID1A with SMARCA2, APC with TMED10, and several KRAS or conditional EGFR contexts. The most informative next registered analysis is a direct CDKN2A-by-TP53-loss interaction test for MDM2 to assess whether the validated CDKN2A effect is formally modified by TP53 status; the already registered screen-quality interaction probes for USP7 and STAT3 are also valuable follow-ups. All conclusions are associations in the supplied dataset and do not establish causality or external generalizability.",
